y long time even from the first  indictment it could be years until the  entire Trump Russia scandal is resolved  so the 2018 midterms could actually have  a major impact on what  what happens with Trump Russia because  depending on whether it's Democrats or  Republicans that control the house from  2018 to 2020 depending on whether it's  Democrats or Republicans that control  the house of the Senate rather between  2018 and 2020 that could have a major  impact on the future of the Trump Russia  investigation because a  republican-controlled house might react  to what is the eventual report from  special prosecutor Robert Moeller very  differently than a democratically  controlled house same thing with the  Senate so we need to be thinking about  2018  not only because midterms are  opportunities for the opposition party  to make gains not only because we need  to do everything we can to prevent  Donald Trump's harebrained ideas from  becoming reality but also because it  could impact whether we eventually  actually see justice in the Trump Russia  investigation and then along these lines  I find it truly stunning that we have a  sitting active President of the United  States whose former campaign Chairman is  arguably about to be indicted whose  former national security adviser is also  facing criminal indictment and there are  people who either number one don't think  this is a big deal number two think it's  fake news or number three don't even  know about it  because the Trump Russia scandal is  barely being mentioned as anything other  than a left-wing conspiracy theory on  right-wing media a lot of people don't  even know what's going on how do you  feel though about these representatives  like Richard Blumenthal and Mark Warner  going out there and giving updates on  the investigation I just think that the  Republican charge is that this is all a  witch-hunt and it's all about political  posturing and they kind of validated I  would just like to see you know 